s=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for cooking</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">6</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">strips</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">bacon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">add crunch and flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">shredded Monterey Jack cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for cheesiness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">tomatoes</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">sliced, for freshness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">green onions</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">sliced, for garnish</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-12114-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"12114\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For searing the chicken</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking sheet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For baking the chicken</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-12114-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-12114-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"12114\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12114-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat your oven to 375°F. This will ensure your chicken bakes perfectly!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12114-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Season the chicken breasts with salt, pepper, garlic powder, and paprika. Make sure to coat them evenly for the best flavor!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12114-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a skillet over medium-high heat, warm some olive oil. Sear the chicken for 3-4 minutes on each side until they are golden brown.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12114-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place the seared chicken on a baking sheet. Top each breast with crumbled cooked bacon, tomato slices, and a generous amount of shredded cheese.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12114-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bake in the preheated oven for 10-12 minutes. The cheese should be melted, and the chicken should reach an internal temperature of 165°F.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12114-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Garnish with sliced green onions and serve immediately. Enjoy your delicious Monterey Chicken!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-12114-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>350</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these delicious ingredients to make your Monterey Chicken!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Monterey-Chicken.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for Monterey chicken displayed on a kitchen table, including chicken, spices, bacon, cheese, tomatoes, and green onions.\" class=\"wp-image-12112\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Monterey-Chicken.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Monterey-Chicken-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>4 boneless skinless <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken_as_food\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chicken </a>breasts</strong> – main protein</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>salt</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>garlic powder</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>paprika</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tbsp olive oil</strong> – for cooking</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>6 strips bacon</strong> – add crunch and flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup shredded Monterey Jack cheese</strong> – for cheesiness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tomatoes</strong> – sliced, for freshness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 green onions</strong> – sliced, for garnish</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-monterey-chicken\"><strong>How to Make Monterey Chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful Monterey Chicken recipe is a breeze to prepare! With a total preparation time of about 10 minutes, cooking time of 15-20 minutes, and an extra baking time of 10-12 minutes, you&#8217;ll have a delicious meal ready in no time!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Preparation-Steps-for-Monterey-Chicken.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of Monterey chicken, showcasing seasoning, searing, and baking process.\" class=\"wp-image-12113\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Preparation-Steps-for-Monterey-Chicken.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Preparation-Steps-for-Monterey-Chicken-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 375°F. This will ensure your chicken bakes perfectly!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Season the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season the chicken breasts with salt, pepper, garlic powder, and paprika. Make sure to coat them evenly for the best flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Sear the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a skillet over medium-high heat, warm some olive oil. Sear the chicken for 3-4 minutes on each side until they are golden brown.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Prepare for Baking</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the seared chicken on a baking sheet. Top each breast with crumbled cooked bacon, tomato slices, and a generous amount of shredded cheese.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Bake the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake in the preheated oven for 10-12 minutes. The cheese should be melted, and the chicken should reach an internal temperature of 165°F.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Garnish with sliced green onions and serve immediately. Enjoy your delicious Monterey Chicken!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>12 minutes (baking)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>42 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot and cheesy with fresh toppings!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-monterey-chicken\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making monterey chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose fresh bell peppers for vibrant color and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cook the chicken until golden brown for a delicious crust.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use shredded cheese for even melting and gooeyness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the dish rest for a few minutes before serving to enhance flavors.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-monterey-chicken\"><strong>How to Serve this monterey chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve over a bed of fluffy rice or quinoa for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a fresh garden salad drizzled with a light vinaigrette.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with sliced avocado for a creamy texture and added flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with warm, crusty bread to soak up the delicious juices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a fun twist, serve in taco shells with your favorite toppings.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Complement with steamed broccoli or green beans for a colorful plate.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can prepare and store Monterey Chicken for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the dish to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the dish completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a freezer-safe container or heavy-duty freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat until warmed through.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use a microwave in short intervals, stirring in between.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is a monterey chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Monterey chicken is a delicious dish that typically features grilled chicken breasts topped with a blend of cheese, bacon, and bell peppers. This hearty meal is known for its savory flavors and is often served with sides like rice or vegetables, making it a satisfying option for dinner any night of the week.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What is Taylor Swift&#8217;s favorite chicken dinner?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While Taylor Swift has mentioned various favorite foods, she has a particular fondness for chicken and often enjoys a classic chicken dinner. However, specific details about her favorite chicken dish aren&#8217;t widely publicized, so it’s best to stick with your own favorites when preparing a meal inspired by her tastes!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What to pair with monterey chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Monterey chicken pairs wonderfully with a variety of sides. Consider serving it with a fresh garden salad, steamed vegetables, or creamy mashed potatoes. For a heartier option, you might also enjoy it with rice or quinoa, which can soak up the delicious flavors of the dish.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What are popular chicken Monterey toppings?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Popular toppings for Monterey chicken include melted cheese (like Monterey Jack or cheddar), crispy bacon, sautéed bell peppers, and sometimes even avocado or fresh herbs. These toppings not only enhance the flavor but also add a delightful texture to the dish, making it even more enjoyable!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to savor the delightful flavors of Monterey Chicken! This cheesy, bacon-topped dish is not just easy to whip up, but it also brings a warm, comforting vibe to your dinner table. So gather your loved ones, enjoy the simple pleasures of cooking, and relish every bite of this rewarding meal. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
